{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions","id":1143328,"title":"Ghoul questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-23T14:42:42-07:00","id":1143328,"title":"Ghoul questions","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> These questions about Ghouls and &quot;Oath of Matrimony&quot; keep popping into my head, and would like some help answering them: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If an Ghoul obtains a Template, does it lose its Ghoul qualities?</li> <li>Can a creature with a Template become a Ghoul?</li> <li>Can a Ghoul learn Devotions?</li> <li>If a Ghoul enters an &quot;Oath of Matrimony&quot; does it become a full fledged Vampire?</li> <li>If a mortal or another supernatural enters an &quot;Oath of Matrimony&quot; do they gain Vampiric benefits and vulnerabilities?</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-23-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T14:59:43-07:00","id":1143333,"title":"","content":"1. Yes.<br /> 2. No.<br /> 3. Yes.<br /> 4. No?<br /> 5. No.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T16:03:56-07:00","id":1143343,"title":"","content":"Two clarifications and one correction:<br /> 3. It's actually not stated whether or not ghouls can learn Devotions, but since they're humans with added abilities you could make the argumant that they probably shouldn't have any abilities that aren't explicitly stated.<br /> 4. Very unlikely since it's stated that non-Kindred might just develop a Kindred-specific trait or two.<br /> 5. Quite possibly since it's stated that non-Kindred might develop a Kindred-specific trait or two. They probably won't get the whole package, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 09-23-2017, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T16:13:21-07:00","id":1143347,"title":"","content":"I would say no Devotions for Ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T16:17:13-07:00","id":1143349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1143347#post1143347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say no Devotions for Ghoul.</div> </div> </div> </div>The pre-requisite for devotions is disciplines, and ghouls can learn any. Hence they can have devotions, but that would be rarely endorsed by a domitor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T17:29:02-07:00","id":1143357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1143349#post1143349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The pre-requisite for devotions is disciplines, and ghouls can learn any. Hence they can have devotions, but that would be rarely endorsed by a domitor.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, revenants can learn disciplines, but they cannot learn devotions. So, that could mean ghouls probably can't learn devotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T17:34:58-07:00","id":1143358,"title":"","content":"We've had a massive argument about whether ghouls can learn devotions or not before.<br /> <br /> I'm on team &quot;no&quot;, largely because of the revenant thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T11:41:05-07:00","id":1143520,"title":"","content":"Unless were going to have ghouls able to do something revenants cant... which is all kind of messed up... then again white wolf/Onyx Path has ALWAYS been all kinds of messed up so :Shrugs:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T18:13:13-07:00","id":1143633,"title":"","content":"Why wouldn't Ghouls be able to do things Revenants can't? Revenants are awful in every way. They have all the weaknesses of vampires and more, and not all of the benefits Ghouls get. Ghouls don't lose their Vitae daily, for example.<br /> <br /> And that's not a bad thing. Revenants are supposed to be awful. They're supposed to be something bad that Vampires try to avoid creating. They're a mistake. They're accidents and Masquerade risks.<br /> <br /> People like to act like there's a hierarchy, where Revenants are closer to &quot;true&quot; vampires and therefore are &quot;better&quot; than Ghouls, but there's no evidence for this position. Revenants are a reason to not be sloppy with your feeding and a reason to avoid killing people willy-nilly. Creating a revenant is a mistake, not a goal. Something to be avoided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T21:40:26-07:00","id":1143669,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> Ghouls also have the chance to become Revenants when they die, so what happens to their devotions if they become a Revenant? Are they simply incapable of using it till they attain full Kindred-dom, or can they still use it and are just unable to learn new ones, or is it something else entirely?<br /> <br /> I personally think it just makes things a bit simpler by saying that ghouls can't learn devotions.<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone was acting like Revenants are above ghouls, seeing as both are not fun positions to be in. I just think that Revenants not being able to learn devotions kind of supports Ghouls not being able to learn them; Revenants are closer to the Kindred condition by being dead and all, unlike ghouls who are still alive and must be fed vitae while Revenants can feed on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T03:42:32-07:00","id":1143719,"title":"","content":"Yes, ravenants are errors, soemthing not wished, non the less they are more powerful and closer to vampires than Ghoul. I definetly would state for no devotions for Ghoul. In my view Devotions are something very exclusive to Vampiric condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T04:01:25-07:00","id":1143724,"title":"","content":"Ok, as far as the &quot;lose vitae daily&quot; thing, I think you're overlooking the fact that it does different things. Ghouls need one vitae a month to use their vampiric abilities. Revenants lose all their vitae every night as that same power <i>animates their body because they're a walking corpse.</i><br /> <br /> Most of the benefits of being a ghoul are due to being <i>alive. </i>Devotions have nothing to do with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T06:11:10-07:00","id":1143751,"title":"","content":"Above, on par, more or less powerful.... I think that's just semantics. The mere fact that a comparison to revenants is being brought up is support for Maina's point - there's no such thing as a template hierarchy, and trying to suggest that because both are &quot;below&quot; true kindred, there has to be some parity in ability has nothing support. That's not how the rules work. &quot;Because revenants&quot; is not an explanation for anything but revenants. It has no impact on what ghouls, dhampirs or any other half-damned type.<br /> <br /> There's no measurement of how close you are to a &quot;true vampire.&quot; Just different rules and abilities for each state of being. Each of the half-damned has different themes and rules that should have no impact on how other half-damned work. Otherwise... should we start trying to figure out how mandrakes are using Disciplines? Celerity vines!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-25-2017, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T18:13:52-07:00","id":1143931,"title":"","content":"Learning Disciplines: Ghouls may learn Disciplines under<br /> the same rules as Kindred. They may not learn Coils or Scales<br /> of the Dragon. -- page 297<br /> <br /> <br /> Many vampires develop the abilities listed here for each<br /> Discipline, but some manifest new powers of the Blood. These<br /> new Discipline techniques, called Devotions, can manifest<br /> spontaneously in some Kindred, or can be developed by<br /> careful honing of Discipline abilities ---- page 142<br /> <br /> Devotions are pieces of Disciplines .. Ghouls can learn disciplines the way a vampire does except where listed ( the Ordo ). Hence. ... A ghoul can learn a devotion. Like a ghoul Can learn Majesty which involves the discipline techniques Awe, Confidant, Green Eyes, Loyalty? Idol, and ... Summoning.<br /> <br /> I am not sure why people use the argument a revenant cant so a ghoul cant. They each have their own SEPARATE how to sections which describes what they can and can not do. Ghoul explicitly states they can learn the exact same thing a vampire can EXCEPT this one thing, which is Coils and Scales of the Ordo. Not They can learn the exact same thing a vampire can Except these two things scales and devotions.<br /> <br /> Revenants does the same thing. They can learn disciplines EXCEPT these things... &quot;They may never learn Devotions, blood sorceries, or Coils or Scales of the Dragon.&quot; Right there already It says Ghouls CAN learn Blood Sorcery and Revenants can not. Already they are two different entities. Like a ghost is not a giest but they are both spirits. They are related but not quite the same thing. They should not have the same rules... especially when the book already tells us what to do.<br /> <br /> I dont think one is more or less a vampire. Ghouls Can hold and store vitae Revenants can not. Ghouls can learn Blood Sorcery Revenants can not. Revenants can Diablerize, ghouls can not. Revenants have blood Sympathy Ghouls (normally) Do not. <br /> <br /> It's like a family tree Vampire is the top and it can spawn two types of things. Say a boy and a girl next to each other. Equal but different in their own ways. It's not a ladder with a vampire, revenant then a ghoul. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 09-25-2017, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T19:02:24-07:00","id":1143940,"title":"","content":"I run Ghouls being able to learn Devotions <i>from</i> someone else(with Vitae cost in addition to XP) but not develop new ones themselves, as they are not close enough to true blood to have a &quot;natural&quot; affinity to spontaneously develop such things.<br /> Also, with them generally being slaves and unable to obtain Vitae at their leisure, they likely won't have the extra Vitae to burn in trial and error type experimentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T00:25:34-07:00","id":1143988,"title":"","content":"I think we already had this argument before, and I believe the main conclusion was &quot;where is Half Damned when you need it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T00:41:43-07:00","id":1143992,"title":"","content":"If Devotions were simply discipline techniques there would be absolutely no reason that revenants could not learn them. Therefore they must be a distinct thing. <i>Therefore</i> the line that ghouls can learn disciplines does <i>not</i> extend to them. Ghouls can learn <i>disciplines</i> like vampires. And devotions, while similar, are <i>not</i> disciplines on a fundamental level. <i>Because if they were then revenants would be able to learn them. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T02:27:32-07:00","id":1144002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1143992#post1143992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Because if they were then revenants would be able to learn them. </i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why?<br /> <br /> This is making some assumptions about the setting without justification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T02:55:26-07:00","id":1144007,"title":"","content":"If a thing can learn one set of powers, but not another set of powers, then the two sets of powers must have some sort of distinction that means they are not entirely interchangeable. <br /> <br /> If this is not the case, then anything that can use one must be able to use the other.<br /> <br /> Because that's how being the same thing works. <br /> <br /> This is not a difficult concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T03:12:12-07:00","id":1144014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1143992#post1143992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Devotions were simply discipline techniques there would be absolutely no reason that revenants could not learn them. Therefore they must be a distinct thing. <i>Therefore</i> the line that ghouls can learn disciplines does <i>not</i> extend to them. Ghouls can learn <i>disciplines</i> like vampires. And devotions, while similar, are <i>not</i> disciplines on a fundamental level. <i>Because if they were then revenants would be able to learn them. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>The book is clear on the subject: Revenants explicitly call devotions as off limit. Ghouls do not get that distinction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T03:31:08-07:00","id":1144016,"title":"","content":"The book is written by human beings, they can miss something. If something is not logical probably is a developer omission. By the way we are all smart people able to take their own decision: someone can state: no devotion for Ghoul because its logical conclusions, other can state for yes because Book simply don't say they can't.<br /> If any developers will tell us, here or in a FAQ, what their intentions about this topic were, we could have an official interpretation.<br /> <br /> Until then, for now, as I said for me Devotion are outside Ghoul's capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-26-2017, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T04:06:04-07:00","id":1144017,"title":"","content":"Revenants are vampires except where noted. Ghouls are human except where noted. So omissions in their write-up should be taken to mean opposite things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T04:11:47-07:00","id":1144018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144016#post1144016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If something is not logical probably is a developer omission.</div> </div> </div> </div> The argument that ghouls can't use devotions because revenants is, in itself, not logical. There's no reason to suggest a comparison. Ghouls and revenants serve completely different positions, not only in terms of story, but game design. Revenants are designed to have a shelf life, either as PCs or NPCs. They don't develop devotions as a function of this hectic short life span. Ghouls are designed to be long term PCs with their own advantages that make them fit in vampire society for hundreds of years. There's no reason to create a comparison in the first place.<br /> <br /> And, frankly, trying to blame the writers and developers is nothing more than shameful. &quot;Its not written the way I want, therefore someone made a mistake.&quot; Two different writers detailed these two different critters. They each had different ideas on what they wanted to do, and each has separate value.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way we are all smart people able to take their own decision: someone can state: no devotion for Ghoul because its logical conclusions, other can state for yes because Book simply don't say they can't. </div> </div> </div> No, you can't say its logical, because its entirely illogical. That's not how logic works.<br /> <br /> You want to make it a houserule? That's fine. Go for it. But it remains a houserule, and not the default, and suggesting that it is the default is just going to confuse people.<br /> <br /> This entire argument revolves around some kind of D&amp;D-esk &quot;all races must be equal&quot; white-room balance mindset. Onyx Path has never once subcribed to that philosphy, and developers have often flat out said that balance is a myth, and not something they subscribe to. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If any developers will tell us, here or in a FAQ, what their intentions about this topic were, we could have an official interpretation.<br /> <br /> Until then, for now, as I said for me Devotion are outside Ghoul's capabilities. </div> </div> </div> They did. Its called the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-26-2017, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T04:22:17-07:00","id":1144020,"title":"","content":"It doesn't say revenants <i>don't</i> develop devotions, it says they <i>can't. </i> Their lifespan is irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T05:22:49-07:00","id":1144031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144018#post1144018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The argument that ghouls can't use devotions because revenants is, in itself, not logical. There's no reason to suggest a comparison. Ghouls and revenants serve completely different positions, not only in terms of story, but game design. Revenants are designed to have a shelf life, either as PCs or NPCs. They don't develop devotions as a function of this hectic short life span. Ghouls are designed to be long term PCs with their own advantages that make them fit in vampire society for hundreds of years. There's no reason to create a comparison in the first place.<br /> <br /> And, frankly, trying to blame the writers and developers is nothing more than shameful. &quot;Its not written the way I want, therefore someone made a mistake.&quot; Two different writers detailed these two different critters. They each had different ideas on what they wanted to do, and each has separate value.<br /> <br /> No, you can't say its logical, because its entirely illogical. That's not how logic works.<br /> <br /> You want to make it a houserule? That's fine. Go for it. But it remains a houserule, and not the default, and suggesting that it is the default is just going to confuse people.<br /> <br /> This entire argument revolves around some kind of D&amp;D-esk &quot;all races must be equal&quot; white-room balance mindset. Onyx Path has never once subcribed to that philosphy, and developers have often flat out said that balance is a myth, and not something they subscribe to.<br /> <br /> They did. Its called the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I said logical/non logical I was simply referring to the attempt, made by Elfive and other, to explain their point of view compared this with the argumentation that they can just because the book doesn't say ghoul CAN'T learn devotions. I don't want to say which argumentation is correct but it's a matter of fact that logical argumentation comes when you try to demonstrate it (right or wrong), while just saying: &quot;the book doesn't exclude they can so they can&quot; it's not a logical argumentation (even if this is the intention of the developers and he is right in its interpretation). I don't want to blame anyone I just pointed out what is my view and position in this discussion, that's all.<br /> <br /> Book doesn''t state humans can't learn devotions as well, so they could <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just kidding :P<br /> <br /> EDIT: I want to clarify that I'm not blaming the dev. This is just a your wrong interpretation I just sayd: it could be (different from: iIT IS) a Dev omission that, as human beings, are allowed to miss to specifiy everything in a so huge game system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-26-2017, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T06:58:28-07:00","id":1144044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144031#post1144031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I said logical/non logical I was simply referring to the attempt,</div> </div> </div> </div> You're the one who brought up logic. No one else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't want to say which argumentation is correct but it's a matter of fact that logical argumentation comes when you try to demonstrate it (right or wrong), while just saying: &quot;the book doesn't exclude they can so they can&quot; it's not a logical argumentation (even if this is the intention of the developers and he is right in its interpretation). </div> </div> </div> You claim to not saying which argument is correct, but you are making phrases about which &quot;side&quot; is logical. Your language here is extremely biased in favor of your stated position, back on the first page. You are flat out saying that people who disagree with you are not being logical, which is just a thinly veiled insult.<br /> <br /> And you are also mischaracterizing the arguments that don't agree with you. The argument for ghoul devotions has several components. One is that devotions are flat out called a type of Discipline by the book, and ghouls can learn and discipline in the same manner as their master's clan. Ghouls can learn Cruac (and have examples in books) while revenants are banned, so clear examples of ghouls learning things revenants can't is firmly established. Ghouls have examples of things listed that they cannot learn; logically, if ghouls couldn't learn devotions, it should be here, and yet its not. Its one thing if no exclusions were listed, but when there are things listed? Clearly, consideration about what ghouls can and cannot do was given, and trying to suggest that the writers didn't include what you want is an oversight instead of deliberate choice is misleading at best.<br /> <br /> You call your argument logical, and yet, you have no stated reason beyond &quot;because revenant.&quot; That's not logic. So, please. If you really want to portray your argument as logical, as you clearly stated above, then lets hear it. The actual logic, in detail. Tell us why the revenants' inability to learn devotions should apply to ghouls, while we should ignore the established precident of ghouls learning Cruac and revenants being unable to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't want to blame anyone I just pointed out what is my view and position in this discussion, that's all.<br /> <br /> Book doesn''t state humans can't learn devotions as well, so they could <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just kidding :P </div> </div> </div> And yet, you continue to belittle and mischaracterize the argument that doesn't agree with yours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: I want to clarify that I'm not blaming the dev. This is just a your wrong interpretation I just sayd: it could be (different from: iIT IS) a Dev omission that, as human beings, are allowed to miss to specifiy everything in a so huge game system. </div> </div> </div> Sure you are. You brought it up as a possible explanation for why ghouls aren't listed as being unable to learn devotions, despite your stance being &quot;logical.&quot; You are implying that it was an oversight to not list it, a mistake. That is absolutely blame. You might be using it as an excuse to try and shield your stance instead of attacking, but its still a form of blame.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144020#post1144020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">It doesn't say revenants </span><i>don't</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> develop devotions, it says they </span><i>can't. </i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Their lifespan is irrelevant.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">.... seriously? The very first line I said in that post had &quot;can't learn devotions.&quot;<br /> <br /> I then proceeded to talk about things from a metagame-design level, and why the choice to disallow devotions was made for revenants. &quot;Don't&quot; is an apparopriate word for talking from the design level. At no point have I implied that revenants have the possibility of developing devotions. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-26-2017, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T07:29:32-07:00","id":1144054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144044#post1144044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure you are. You brought it up as a possible explanation for why ghouls aren't listed as being unable to learn devotions, despite your stance being &quot;logical.&quot; You are implying that it was an oversight to not list it, a mistake. That is absolutely blame. You might be using it as an excuse to try and shield your stance instead of attacking, but its still a form of blame.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will let fall the rest of discussion since I said what I thought and you are free to interpret it as you wish. I don't mind. Maybe it's also my fault since English is not my native language and actually my English level really sucks.<br /> <br /> But, again, NO! I gave my opinion and specified that it can be wrong as well as could be your. I just told that, in a so huge game system, is normal for any human being, to miss/forget/whatever to state every single aspect of the game, or the ERRATA, FAQ would not exist at all. Saying so, I'm not blaming anyone, I'm simply answering to those that think to be right just because it is not explicitly written that Devotion are not allowed for Ghoul, pointing out that this is not an exhaustive explanation since it is POSSIBLE that it's just an omission. If you think this is a kind of attempt to blaming the developer I just can say you are wrong, it is actually the opposite. But for me this discussion ends here. I'm sorry to have been misunderstood but again, don't try to give your own interpretation to my words as a fact while I'm expressly saying it's not what I meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T07:35:03-07:00","id":1144058,"title":"","content":"just to note- as Half Damned is going to give an in depth look at the Revenant existence, one which is equal to Ghouls and Dampyrs (which are both fully playable options), I believe that the argument about Revenants meant to have &quot;sort shelf life&quot; is not fully correct. You are making an assumption about the writer/developer's intentions, which may be incorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T07:40:23-07:00","id":1144060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144044#post1144044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At no point have I implied that revenants have the possibility of developing devotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never claimed you did. You actually <i>did</i>, because &quot; They don't develop devotions as a function of this hectic short life span.&quot; does kind of imply that if they lived longer they would, but I never claimed that until just now.<br /> <br /> The point is that their outright inability to do so must be intrinsic, so their narrative role is not, in my opinion, a relevant factor here. They <i>are</i> more vampire than ghouls, by virtue of being actual undead blood-sucking monsters. So there's no real reason for them to be unable to use devotions under the assumptions by which you and others are granting them to ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T08:09:39-07:00","id":1144071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144060#post1144060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never claimed you did. You actually <i>did</i>, because &quot; They don't develop devotions as a function of this hectic short life span.&quot; does kind of imply that if they lived longer they would, but I never claimed that until just now.<br /> <br /> The point is that their outright inability to do so must be intrinsic, so their narrative role is not, in my opinion, a relevant factor here. They <i>are</i> more vampire than ghouls, by virtue of being actual undead blood-sucking monsters. So there's no real reason for them to be unable to use devotions under the assumptions by which you and others are granting them to ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you want to add anything on the several other points <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> made? No? Ok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T08:12:28-07:00","id":1144072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1143992#post1143992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Devotions were simply discipline techniques there would be absolutely no reason that revenants could not learn them. Therefore they must be a distinct thing. <i>Therefore</i> the line that ghouls can learn disciplines does <i>not</i> extend to them. Ghouls can learn <i>disciplines</i> like vampires. And devotions, while similar, are <i>not</i> disciplines on a fundamental level. <i>Because if they were then revenants would be able to learn them. </i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The book explicitly says they are part of disciplines, they are disciplines. I even quoted the section of the book that says so. I am not really sure why you don't believe it when I offered word for word proof.<br /> <br /> Also word for word proof offered was that ghouls learn disciplines exactly like kindred EXCEPT where noted. That exception does not note devotions or blood sorcery. They cant even use most of the blood sorcery but they can still learn it. Please offer some Actual book references to support your claims.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To others:<br /> <br /> Again Ghouls can learn blood sorcery and Revenants can not so this whole argument of &quot;Reveants cant learn them so ghouls shouldn't be able to either&quot; has been proven fundamentally wrong with evidence from the book<br /> <br /> <br /> Also someone said that Ghouls are slaves and can only get vitae when allowed so therefore shouldn't be able to learn/develop devotions is not something that is true in all aspects. That is maybe how YOU run ghouls but I guarentee not everyone runs them like that. Not every ghoul is a slave. Not every ghoul is kept on a tiny leash. So making that statement is an opinion not a fact for all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Here is the book Evidence again. Please someone refute this with text evidence rather than opinions based in &quot;Well I think&quot; <br /> <br /> Learning Disciplines: Ghouls may learn Disciplines under<br /> the same rules as Kindred. <b>They may not learn Coils or Scales</b><br /> <b>of the Dragon. -- page 297 ( &lt;-- the one and only exception to the rules of discipline learning for ghouls )</b><br /> <br /> <br /> DEVOTION SECTION OF THE BOOK:<br /> <br /> Many vampires develop the abilities listed here for each<br /> <b>Discipline</b>, but some manifest new powers of the Blood. These<br /> new<b> Discipline techniques</b>, called Devotions, can manifest<br /> spontaneously in some Kindred, or can be developed by<br /> careful honing of<b> Discipline abilities</b> ---- page 142<br /> <br /> ( It called them discipline abilities/techniques 3 times in that section )<br /> Awe and Summoning are discipline abilities of Majesty. Summoning is a Devotion to the discipline Majesty ( or Dominate )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 09-26-2017, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T09:13:01-07:00","id":1144095,"title":"","content":"We've been over this before, in the last thread. I'm basing a lot of my interpretation on the <i>exact same passages you are.</i> The only difference is that when I read &quot;disciplines&quot; I interpret that to mean <i>only</i> disciplines, with dots. Because, despite the book describing devotions as &quot;discipline techniques&quot; they can't <i>simply</i> be that because if that's all there were there would be <i>no justifiable metaphysical reason</i> for <i>anything </i>to be able to learn one but not the other. <br /> <br /> The very fact that revenants can learn one but not the other means that they are <i>distinct things</i>. So if the book doesn't <i>say</i> ghouls can learn &quot;disciplines and devotions&quot; then it doesn't <i>mean</i> ghouls can learn disciplines and devotions. <br /> <br /> But that's just my 2 cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T10:57:13-07:00","id":1144127,"title":"","content":"I want to build a lego house. The pieces the directions say that I can use are yellow, green, blue, and orange.<br /> <br /> Now the directions say I can build another lego house and use all the same directions except that I am not allowed to use orange. The way that critical reading goes means that I am still allowed to use yellow, green and blue. I just can't use orange.<br /> <br /> If I am allowed to build a third house and I am allowed to use the same things as the first house but this time I am not allowed to use yellow and green. It implies I am allowed to use Blue and Orange. I cant say... because I wasn't allowed to use orange for my second house I shouldnt be able to with my third house. That makes no sense what so ever.<br /> <br /> All the houses are going to be uniquely different from each other because they were allowed to use different tools, but that doesnt make the second house any less of a house than third is...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: :: Below are secondary questions: <br /> <br /> Why can a revenant not learn blood sorcery where a ghoul can? There is no justifiable metaphysical reason for this either.... But there it is in the book.<br /> Also any vampire can learn any discipline and devotion and coil and sorcery... except where listed(blooodline specific ).. Why wouldn't that apply to the ghoul where it says they learn exactly like a vampire, except this one thing (coils) ..?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":"Edit: :: Below are secondary questions: 09-26-2017, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T11:20:33-07:00","id":1144134,"title":"","content":"Ah, no. That's not what happening here. The first house uses blue, green, yellow and orange. The second house says you can use blue. The third house says you can blue and clarifies that you can't use yellow and orange.<br /> <br /> You then argued that the third house can use green because green is a shade of blue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T11:31:28-07:00","id":1144137,"title":"","content":"There is a book coming out that's going to answer your questions more definitively than arguing on the forum will.<br /> <br /> Though you are free to toss the rules and reasons within in favor of your own setting if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T11:37:24-07:00","id":1144141,"title":"","content":"Yeah, honestly when I mentioned on page 1 that the last time we discussed this it devolved into a massive argument, I didn't mean &quot;lets start that shit again here&quot;.<br /> <br /> Largely because I always get sucked into this crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T11:54:35-07:00","id":1144153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144134#post1144134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, no. That's not what happening here. The first house uses blue, green, yellow and orange. The second house says you can use blue. The third house says you can blue and clarifies that you can't use yellow and orange.<br /> <br /> You then argued that the third house can use green because green is a shade of blue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am seriously questioning your reading skills. I mean no offense... but where did I say that the third house can't use yellow and Orange??<br /> <br /> The second house said I can use everything the first house did except for orange.. how does it limit that to only blue?? <br /> <br /> How on earth did your logic get there? <br /> <br /> <br /> - reads and rereads what I said. - <br /> House 1 - blue, green, yellow and orange<br /> House 2 - blue, green, yellow and orange, but actually not orange = blue, green, yellow<br /> House 3 - blue, green, yellow and orange, But actually not green or yellow = blue and orange<br /> <br /> If you want to interpret that the second house can only use blue and that the third house you can use only blue... Then.. I guess that's your right???<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:01:36-07:00","id":1144156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144153#post1144153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am seriously questioning your reading skills. I mean no offense... but where did I say that the third house can't use yellow and Orange??<br /> <br /> The second house said I can use everything the first house did except for orange.. how does it limit that to only blue??<br /> <br /> How on earth did your logic get there?<br /> <br /> <br /> - reads and rereads what I said. -<br /> House 1 - blue, green, yellow and orange<br /> House 2 - blue, green, yellow and orange, but actually not orange = blue, green, yellow<br /> House 3 - blue, green, yellow and orange, But actually not green or yellow = blue and orange<br /> <br /> If you want to interpret that the second house can only use blue and that the third house you can use only blue... Then.. I guess that's your right???<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think Elfive was providing the reading of the book according to your example to clarify what are the changes between your two points of view, not the reading of your example as you wrote it.<br /> But I could be wrong, in such case forgive me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-26-2017, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:28:59-07:00","id":1144166,"title":"","content":"But that's not how you are suppose to read things in cases of &quot;Follow that, except for this&quot; You're not suppose to say &quot;Well My brother can, so why cant I?&quot; You are literally suppose to follow that except where listed.. if said things are not listed it is implied that they are just the same as the original. <br /> <br /> <br /> If something isnt included on the no list... then it's implied that it can be used. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am asking if that is wrong and we are suppose to go with the motto &quot;If Revenants can't, then Ghouls can't&quot;<br /> <br /> &gt;&gt; Why Can ghouls use blood sorcery and revenants can not? &lt;&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T13:20:46-07:00","id":1144183,"title":"","content":"Yes, I was reframing your example to how I was interpreting the ghoul question. Sorry, I thought that would be obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T13:54:36-07:00","id":1144191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144183#post1144183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I was reframing your example to how I was interpreting the ghoul question. Sorry, I thought that would be obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesn't make sense... you speak of mixing colors and creating shades, but you missed a huge critical piece of the metaphorical puzzle, which I think is happening when you read the book's text. I said pieces allowed. Not colors allowed<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>&quot; Ah, no. That's not what happening here. The first house uses blue, green, yellow and orange. The second house says you can use blue. The third house says you can blue and clarifies that you can't use yellow and orange.<br /> <br /> You then argued that the third house can use green because green is a shade of blue. &quot;</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I didn't make an argument that the third house can use green because it is a shade of blue. I stated Here are the building blocks of the house. These are the ones you can use except where noted. There were no arguments, only statements of what is... and what is not for three entirely separate yet related entities. You're adding things that don't belong and that werent stated. Like the third house not being able to use orange. No where does it say that. You are only saying that because it's related to yellow.. But their (yellow and orange )relation is utterly irrelevant in the case of building the house.<br /> <br /> If that is what you were doing for the ghoul... then in both cases you just proved how your analysis of the text is incorrect.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> But really just like any other game. And as you ( Elfive) and others have stated, do what works for you at your table. Or even your game. If it works for one game and not the other. Do whatever you want as long as you're having fun. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 09-26-2017, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T14:38:33-07:00","id":1144201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144166#post1144166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;&gt; Why Can ghouls use blood sorcery and revenants can not? &lt;&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably because ghouls have a more direct connection to Kindred, while revenants are still proto-Kindred.<br /> <br /> But alternatively there's the obvious 'there's something wrong with them,' represented mechanically by their inability to keep Vitae.<br /> <br /> Like I implied before, however, all the reasons in the world won't matter if people don't like them. If you want an official answer, it should be in the upcoming Half-Damned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T11:09:29-07:00","id":1144851,"title":"","content":"I know this is a few days late, but just dropping by to let you know that ghouls *can* learn devotions. I know it isn't explicitly stated in the core, but the intention was not to deny it to them. So sayeth the developer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll make sure there's some kind of explicit statement in Half-Damned for people who don't read the forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T12:45:15-07:00","id":1144893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144851#post1144851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is a few days late, but just dropping by to let you know that ghouls *can* learn devotions. I know it isn't explicitly stated in the core, but the intention was not to deny it to them. So sayeth the developer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll make sure there's some kind of explicit statement in Half-Damned for people who don't read the forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only logical conclusion, despite others' feelings otherwise.<br /> <br /> How feelings and logic get mixed up is probably one of the great causes of much misunderstanding in our many, shared, worlds.<br /> <br /> Gotta thank others, specially <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a> that I remember from a previous round of this discussion, for carrying the torch of reason. I had given up and decided to stay away from the discussion. (Maybe that was a wiser idea than posting, hmmm...) lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 09-28-2017, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}